<title>JAPAN: TEPCO 1997 reactor maintenance closure schedule.</title>
<headline>TEPCO 1997 reactor maintenance closure schedule.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tokyo Electric Power Co Inc (TEPCO) said on Monday that 13 out of its 16 nuclear reactors were scheduled to be closed for routine maintenance checks this year.</p>
<p>TEPCO also said it was unclear how long 10 out of the 13 would be shut for the checks. The other three have already been shut for routine maintenance.</p>
<p>Routine maintenance closures usually last from 45 days to more than three months, a TEPCO spokesman said.</p>
<p>Details of each reactor's shutdown schedule are as follows:</p>
<p>				-REACTOR  CAPACITY-  -DATE-</p>
<p>				     (1,000 KW)</p>
<p>    Fukushima 1	   No 1     460     none in 1997</p>
<p>				No 2     784     Feb 18 - early June</p>
<p>				No 3     784     from late May</p>
<p>				No 4     784     from mid-Sept</p>
<p>				No 5     784     from late Mar</p>
<p>				No 6   1,100     none in 1997</p>
<p>    Fukushima 2	   No 1   1,100     from late Sept</p>
<p>				No 2   1,100     Jan 31 - mid-Mar</p>
<p>				No 3   1,100     from early May</p>
<p>				No 4   1,100     none in 1997</p>
<p>    Kashiwazaki Kariba  No 1   1,100     from late June</p>
<p>				No 2   1,100     Dec 16, 1996 - mid-Mar</p>
<p>				No 3   1,100     from late Apr</p>
<p>				No 4   1,100     from late Aug</p>
<p>				No 5   1,100     from late Dec</p>
<p>				No 6   1,356     from early Dec</p>
